  "notes": "Compound of {返|へん} (return) + {信|しん} (message, letter). Used as a suru-verb: {返信|へんしん}する (to reply).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {返信|へんしん}する (to reply)\n- {返信|へんしん}が{来|く}る (a reply arrives)\n- {返信|へんしん}が{遅|おそ}い (a reply is late)\n- {返信|へんしん}をもらう (to receive a reply)\n- ご{返信|へんしん} (polite: your reply)\n\nUSAGE:\nNot to be confused with the homophone {変身|へんしん} (transformation). {返信|へんしん} specifically refers to replying to correspondence. For replying in general conversation, {返事|へんじ} is more common. {返答|へんとう} is more formal and used for answering questions directly.",
